---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Vocabulary
description: Minted terms and the extensible code lists for government level and organization classification.
---
<div class="container py-5">
  <h1 class="mb-3">Vocabulary</h1>
  <p class="lead">gov-schema mints nothing schema.org already covers. These code lists are <code>DefinedTermSet</code>s rather than fixed enumerations, because tiers of government differ enormously by country.</p>
  <p class="small"><a href="/v1/govschema.ttl">Download the RDF vocabulary (Turtle)</a></p>

  {% for c in profiles.codelists %}
  <section class="mb-5">
    <h2 class="h4 border-bottom pb-2">{{ c.name }}</h2>
    <p>{{ c.description }}</p>
    <p class="small gs-mono text-body-secondary"><a href="/v1/codelists/{{ c.file }}">{{ c.id }}</a></p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
        <thead><tr><th style="width:18%">Code</th><th style="width:22%">Name</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for t in c.terms %}
          <tr>
            <td><code>{{ t.code }}</code></td>
            <td>{{ t.name }}</td>
            <td class="small">{{ t.description }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
